From e76306b9ad8be7664083505722bc42407d2b7c68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 17:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 076/145] media: meson: vdec: extend the reset discipline to
 VDEC_1

The DMC park/scrub bracket added for VDEC_HEVC applies just as much to
VDEC_1 (MPEG1/2, H.264): a session can end with a sub-engine stuck
mid-transaction, and resetting or power-gating in that state wedges the
unit's DDR-controller port and takes the SoC down past even a hardware
watchdog reset.  VDEC_1 currently has none of the discipline - it fires
a blanket DOS_SW_RESET0 = 0xfffffffc with the port live and no drain of
any kind, which is precisely the pattern that proved lethal on HEVC.

The port to park is DMC_REQ_CTRL BIT(21).  The A311D datasheet's memory
interface chapter names it "ambus chan 5, DOS VDEC interface", and it
is confirmed on silicon: sampling DMC_CHAN_STS per channel, bit 21
reads busy in 72% of samples during an H.264 decode and is completely
idle otherwise, while the VDEC_HEVC channels (axibus 4 "hevc front" and
8 "hevc_b") are idle throughout - and under HEVC exactly the reverse,
at 11.7% and 76.9%.  Pre-G12A parts use bit 13 for the same port; only
G12A+ is wired up here because that is what has been validated.

Since both units now need them, the DMC park/unpark and the G12B DMC
pipeline pulse move to vdec_helpers as mask-taking helpers, and
vdec_hevc.c uses them for its own mask.  No behavioural change there.

VDEC_1 gains:
 - vdec_1_stop_armrisc(): halt MPSR/CPSR and drain the IMEM and LMEM
   DMA engines before anything resets (vendor vdec_stop_armrisc()),
 - a targeted sub-engine reset set - vld(3), vld_part(4), vfifo(5),
   mc(7), dblk(8), pic_dc(9) - per the vendor's vdec_reset_core(),
   notably excluding ddr(13) and mcpu/ccpu(11/12),
 - the park/scrub bracket at both power edges, with the park taken
   before the domain comes up (that register is outside the domain) and
   the scrub run only once memories are powered and isolation removed,
 - the firmware-load poll converted from a bare iteration spin to real
   delays with a 1 s budget; declaring success while the IMEM DMA is
   still running starts the processor on half-loaded microcode.

Validated on a VIM3 (G12B), ACPI mode: H.264 1080p and 4K are
frame-md5 exact against software decode (300/300, 300/300, 150/150),
HEVC 4K Main10 is unregressed at 91 fps, and 30 alternating
VDEC_1/VDEC_HEVC teardown cycles run with zero failures and no kernel
warnings.
